# 🔬 Lab 03 — Edge Detection Techniques and Their Impact on Classification Performance

**HAM10000 Skin-Lesion Dataset** · Sobel · Prewitt · Laplacian · LoG · Canny · SVM · Random Forest · KNN · EfficientNet-B3 · ResNet-50

**Author:** Abdul Rehman (FA23-BAI-036) · Team *Quantum Coders*
**Program:** BS Artificial Intelligence — COMSATS University Islamabad, Wah Campus

---

## 📌 Overview

This lab studies classical **edge detection** and asks whether edge maps are a useful input for **skin-lesion classification**. It continues Lab 01 (raw images) and Lab 02 (image filtering) on the same dataset and classes.

The notebook covers six tasks:

1. Implements first-order (Sobel Gx / Gy / magnitude, Prewitt), second-order (Laplacian, LoG) and multi-stage (Canny) edge detectors.
2. Measures how **Gaussian** and **salt-and-pepper** noise affect each detector, and how **Gaussian / Median** filtering helps.
3. Tunes Canny's **low/high thresholds** and **Gaussian kernel size**, and selects the most useful configuration.
4. Builds three versions of the dataset (Raw, Filtered, Edge) with identical train/val/test splits.
5. Trains and compares **5 classifiers** on all three versions.
6. Visualises the best model with confusion matrices and metric charts.

